.TH GIT-STATUS-PUSH 1 "2026-10-01" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-status-push \- show branch status relative to the push remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git status-push
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-status-push\fR inspects each local branch and reports whether it is ahead,
behind, or up to date with respect to its push remote. It prefers a branch-specific
push remote, then falls back to a repository push default or the configured branch
remote. If a branch has never been pushed, it is marked as such.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git status-push
Display ahead/behind counts for all local branches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-branch (1)
